'''Moon Operators''' are an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was implemented in [[Version 6.10 Update|Version 6.10]] and can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. It is a variant of [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|The Death Moon]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 416
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Moon Operators
|name2 = NERV Moon
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''NERV Moon''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
The Moon Operators' slow ability can be useful in certain situations, coupled with their good range, average DPS and [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] ability.

Unlike their cousin [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|The Chaos Moon]], the Moon Operators are not able to outrange notable enemies due to their lower range, but the Slow ability has a 100% chance in all forms rather just the [[True Form]].

The Slow effect they provide can be used with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to kill [[Bore]]s much more efficiently without Bahamut dying.

Useful early game in your road to obtaining [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] and [[Ururun Cat|Ururun Wolf]] as some stages on the way ([[Mexico (Into the Future)|ITF 3 Mexico]] or [[The Great Escaper]]) have [[Bore]]s protected by a crowd of enemies. Typical [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] crowd-controllers like [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Sorceress/Enchantress Cat]] and [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] are single target while [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] is close ranged. Moon Operators have no problems slowing the Bores in these stages provided they are protected by [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]]. However, once these cats are [[True Form|true formed]] or have Research Up [[Cat Combo]]s like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] or [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] applied in battle, their spammability allows them to outclass the Moon Operators.

